  <metadata>
    <name>S01 Komodo gate and the Mbeliling forest</name>
    <desc>Section 01 of the Flores Race traverse: Leaving the tourist town for the first farm tracks. 101.6 km, +3368 m / -3049 m, starts at km 0 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:57Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.493930" lon="119.875650">
    <ele>27.3</ele>
    <name>Labuan Bajo</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: start | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Race start. Also the region's only airport (Komodo/Labuan Bajo Airport, IATA LBJ) and its busiest port (ferries, Komodo tour boats, Pelni). Fully geared tourist town: dive shops, ATMs, supermarkets, hospitals.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Green</sym>
    <type>anchor/start</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.712000" lon="120.024000">
    <ele>749.7</ele>
    <name>Sano Nggoang</name>
    <desc>km 81.4 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay | position unverified -- Small village on the shore of the Sano Nggoang caldera lake, in the kecamatan of the same name. Basic kiosks only; homestays exist for lake visitors but capacity is small and unconfirmed. Anchor placed on the lake shore;</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.648640" lon="120.010760">
    <ele>345.9</ele>
    <name>Werang</name>
    <desc>km 101.6 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Capital of Sano Nggoang kecamatan: parish church (Santo Klaus), police post, camat office, schools. The practical resupply stop after the lake.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.625900" lon="119.997600">
    <ele>442.7</ele>
    <name>Cunca Rami waterfall</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike, position approximate] A ~30 m waterfall deep in the Mbeliling forest reserve, near Wae Lolos village; local sources put it around 1,200 m but the DEM at this approximate fix reads ~800 m -- location needs a field GPS fix.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/waterfall</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.543300" lon="119.996400">
    <ele>194.3</ele>
    <name>Cunca Wulang canyon</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] A river canyon and waterfall ("moon waterfall") near Wersawe village in the Mbeliling area, ~30 km east of Labuan Bajo; a popular canyoning and cliff-jumping stop, ~200 m elevation.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/waterfall</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.615000" lon="119.975000">
    <ele>1226.0</ele>
    <name>Mbeliling forest</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A ~15,000 ha forest reserve and Important Bird Area west of Ruteng, the highest ground in West Manggarai (~1,275 m); habitat for the Flores hanging parrot, Flores monarch, Flores crow and Flores owl.</desc>
    <sym>Forest</sym>
    <type>poi/forest</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.720000" lon="120.020000">
    <ele>831.0</ele>
    <name>Sano Nggoang crater lake</name>
    <desc>[anchor, position approximate] Flores' largest crater lake, in the Wai Sano caldera, said to be among the world's deepest volcanic lakes (~500-600 m); two solfataras and hot springs on its south-east shore. Exact shoreline pending field verification.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/crater-lake</type>
  </wpt>
